  "title": "Erdős Problem #944",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "A critical vertex, edge, or set of edges, is one whose deletion lowers the chromatic number.\nLet $k\\geq 4$ and $r\\geq 1$. Must there exist a graph $G$ with chromatic number $k$ such that every vertex is critical, yet every critical set of edges has size $>r$?",
